<title>USA: Royal Dutch/Shell sets increased capital outlays.</title>
<headline>Royal Dutch/Shell sets increased capital outlays.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Royal Dutch/Shell Group plans capital spending totaling 8.2 billion stg this year, the group said in a statement made available in New York Thurday.</p>
<p>It said that compares to the 7.8 billion stg (or $12.1 billion) spent last year, which was up three percent from 1995 with increases in exploration and production and in marketing partially offset by a reduction in refining.</p>
<p>The group said the major 1997 increase in exploration spending is again being partially offset by a reduction in refining and marketing.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
